n/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9963060-de5c-5656-9e7e-cf990bd21bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-337668" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6541b6d3-e8ce-576d-b74b-a9972271e9ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6541b6d3-e8ce-576d-b74b-a9972271e9ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309529} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e23049-fb20-55b2-85d3-1a5ea98a7667" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "997b5a05-1cb5-50b9-8355-27cc4f1db1d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/val